+## A throwing `beforeSession`
+
+- A `beforeSession` that throws still rejects the caller's promise with the same error, and fires `onError` with that error and then `afterSession`, on the same session ([validated by: runs onError and afterSession when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L40)).
+- `afterSession` runs after a failed `beforeSession` on purpose: it is the release half of a pair whose allocation half lives in `beforeSession`, and skipping it would leak exactly the resource the pair exists to free. The hook receives no flag saying the turn never started, so it cannot tell "never allocated" from "allocated and finished". What it can assume is that `beforeSession` runs before any user-input rewrite, provider call or tool, so none of those happened in a turn that threw there. A deployer who needs to know whether the session started must record that inside `beforeSession` itself.
+- `sessionStore.save`, when configured, is called on the same path, so a turn whose `beforeSession` threw is saved as well.
+
